        "id": 1951687
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-10T08:57:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To save potential back and forth, as we are going back to the host anyway, you could make a request for both tx and rx buffers at the same time, as soon as one of them failed?\n\n```\nif (ret \u003d\u003d -EFAULT) {\n    req \u003d pkvm_hyp_req_reserve(hyp_vcpu, KVM_HYP_REQ_TYPE_MAP);\n    if (!req || !pkvm_hyp_req_reserve(hyp_vcpu, KVM_HYP_REQ_TYPE_MAP))\n        return -ENOSPC;\n\n    req-\u003emap.guest_ipa \u003d tx;\n    req-\u003emap.size \u003d PAGE_SIZE;\n    \n    req++;\n    req-\u003emap.guest_ipa \u003d rx;\n    req-\u003emap.size \u003d PAGE_SIZE    \n}\n```\n\nBut that\u0027s just a small improvement and I believe this is as also good as it is.",
      "revId": "ee855ee4200983d2f82e79a1d54aae35500aa03d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
